MF= 3 Neutron cross sections                                      8931 1451
  Below 0.6 eV:                                                   8931 1451
    * Elastic scattering cross section is 12.5b calculated from   8931 1451
      scattering radius of 9.962 fm/6/.                           8931 1451
    * Fission cross section is in the 1/v shape.                  8931 1451
      1 mb at 0.0253 eV was estimated from the experimental       8931 1451
      data of < 0.35 mb/7/.                                       8931 1451
    * Capture cross section is in the 1/v shape.                  8931 1451
      Cross section of 800 b at 0.0253 eV was an average value of 8931 1451
      experimental data of Monsecour and de Begge/8/ and          8931 1451
      Cabell/9/.                                                  8931 1451
                                                                  8931 1451
  Above 0.3 eV:                                                   8931 1451
    Cross sections were calculated with CCONE code/6/, except     8931 1451
    for the elastic scattering (MT=2) and fission cross sections  8931 1451
    (MT's=18, 19).                                                8931 1451
                                                                  8931 1451
  MT=1  Total cross section                                       8931 1451
    The cross section was calculated with CC OMP of Soukhovitskii 8931 1451
    et al./10/.                                                   8931 1451
                                                                  8931 1451
  MT= 2 Elastic scattering cross section                          8931 1451
    Calculated as total - non-elastic scattering cross sections.  8931 1451
                                                                  8931 1451
  MT=18,19  Fission cross section, (n,f) cross section            8931 1451
    Shape of 1/v was assumed up to 6.5 eV.                        8931 1451
    From 6.5 eV to 100 keV, a constant value of 6 micro-b was     8931 1451
    assumed.                                                      8931 1451
    Above 170 keV, CCONE calculation was adopted.                 8931 1451
    Experimental data of Kuks et al./11/ were used to adjust      8931 1451
    parameters of CCONE code.                                     8931 1451
                                                                  8931 1451
                                                                  8931 1451
