***************************************************************** 8931 1451
  Calculation with CCONE code                                     8931 1451
***************************************************************** 8931 1451
                                                                  8931 1451
  Models and parameters used in the CCONE/6/ calculation          8931 1451
  1) Coupled channel optical model                                8931 1451
     Levels in the rotational band were included. Optical model   8931 1451
     potential and coupled levels are shown in Table 1.           8931 1451
                                                                  8931 1451
  2) Two-component exciton model/14/                              8931 1451
    * Global parametrization of Koning-Duijvestijn/15/            8931 1451
      was used.                                                   8931 1451
    * Gamma emission channel/16/ was added to simulate direct     8931 1451
      and semi-direct capture reaction.                           8931 1451
                                                                  8931 1451
  3) Hauser-Feshbach statistical model                            8931 1451
    * Moldauer width fluctuation correction/17/ was included.     8931 1451
    * Neutron, gamma and fission decay channel were included.     8931 1451
    * Transmission coefficients of neutrons were taken from       8931 1451
      coupled channel calculation in Table 1.                     8931 1451
    * The level scheme of the target is shown in Table 2.         8931 1451
    * Level density formula of constant temperature and Fermi-gas 8931 1451
      model were used with shell energy correction and collective 8931 1451
      enhancement factor. Parameters are shown in Table 3.        8931 1451
    * Fission channel:                                            8931 1451
      Double humped fission barriers were assumed.                8931 1451
      Fission barrier penetrabilities were calculated with        8931 1451
      Hill-Wheler formula/18/. Fission barrier parameters were    8931 1451
      shown in Table 4. Transition state model was used and       8931 1451
      continuum levels are assumed above the saddles. The level   8931 1451
      density parameters for inner and outer saddles are shown in 8931 1451
      Tables 5 and 6, respectively.                               8931 1451
    * Gamma-ray strength function of Kopecky et al/19/,/20/       8931 1451
      was used. The prameters are shown in Table 7.               8931 1451
